# pixi-policy-pre-commit

A [pre-commit](https://pre-commit.com) hook for [pixi-policy](https://github.com/aesir-oss/pixi-policy). Generated from
pixi-policy's `pre-commit-mirror/` on each release; issues and changes go to that repository. Each tag here installs
the pixi-policy wheel of the same version from PyPI, so nothing is compiled.

```yaml
repos:
  - repo: https://github.com/aesir-oss/pixi-policy-pre-commit
    rev: v@VERSION@
    hooks:
      - id: pixi-policy
```

The hook runs when `pixi.toml`, `pixi.lock`, `pyproject.toml` or `pixi-policy.toml` changes, and checks the workspace
the way `pixi policy` does from the repository root: the nearest `pixi.toml` and the `pixi-policy.toml` beside it. A
commit with an error finding is stopped. `args:` passes any other flag (`--manifest-path app/pixi.toml` for a
workspace below the root, `--policy policies/strict.toml`). See the
[pre-commit section of the docs](https://aesir-oss.github.io/pixi-policy/latest/ci/#a-pre-commit-hook).
